@node Maintenance Groups
@subsection Maintenance Groups
@cindex maintenance groups

The maintenance menu is organized by intent.  Transient levels control
which groups are visible; cycle them with @code{transient-set-level}
(@kbd{C-x l} by default).  Level 1 holds the daily operations, level 3
the database, structure, and data groups, level 5 the integrations
sub-dispatcher, and level 7 the setup and migration sub-dispatcher.

@itemize @bullet
@item
@strong{Issue Lifecycle} --- defer, undefer, delete, promote wisp,
rename, unclaim.
@item
@strong{Views & Reports} --- count, stats, stale, types, lint,
duplicates, orphans, wisps.
@item
@strong{Issue Details} --- children, comments, todo, events, query.
@item
@strong{Events} --- the live timeline and its city twin, and the time
travel commands issue history and rewind.
@item
@strong{Workflow} --- gate, swarm, cook, ship, set-state, the state
menu, conflicts, reclaim, heartbeat.
@item
@strong{Database} --- backup, export JSONL, prune, GC, batch ops,
compact, flatten, ping, doctor, migrate, upgrade, preflight, purge.
@item
@strong{Structure} --- mark duplicate, find duplicates, supersede,
restore, SQL query, rename prefix, forget memory.
@item
@strong{Data & Sync} --- version control, Dolt sync, schema, migrate
personal, branch, diff, history, provenance.
@item
@strong{Integrations} --- Jira, Linear, GitLab, GitHub, repo, ADO,
federation, mail.
@item
@strong{Setup & migration} --- init, init safety, integrations, info,
version, bootstrap, hooks, quickstart, where, context, memories, KV
store, prime, recall, remember, audit, admin, worktrees.
@end itemize

The workflow verbs are described with molecules and agents
(@pxref{Cook Pour and Burn}); the integrations and setup sub-dispatchers
are listed in @ref{Command and Key Reference}.

