@node Terminal Backends
@section Terminal Backends
@cindex terminal backends
@cindex vterm
@cindex ghostel
@cindex eat

Agents and interactive CLIs run in a terminal managed by the EIEIO
terminal subsystem (@code{beads-terminal.el}).  Backends are objects of
type @code{beads-terminal}; each knows how to spawn one program in one
terminal.  They register with @code{beads-terminal-register} and are
selected in ascending priority order by @code{beads-terminal-auto}.  The
built-in backends are @code{vterm}, @code{ghostel}, @code{eat},
@code{ansi-term}, and @code{term}, plus @code{auto}, which never spawns
itself but picks the first available concrete terminal.

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-terminal-register (terminal)
Register TERMINAL in the process-wide registry, replacing any backend with
the same name.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-terminal-get (name)
Return the registered terminal named NAME, or nil.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-terminal-list ()
Return the list of registered terminal backends.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-terminal-run (argv buffer-name &optional dir)
Display the terminal buffer named BUFFER-NAME in DIR, spawning ARGV
through the selected backend if the buffer is not live.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-terminal-attach (session &optional socket dir store)
Attach to the tmux SESSION, optionally on SOCKET and in DIR, for STORE.
@end deftypefn

@defvr {User Option} beads-terminal-backend
The preferred terminal backend, or nil to auto-detect.  When nil, the
backends are tried in order: @code{vterm}, @code{ghostel},
@code{eat}, @code{ansi-term}, @code{term}.
@end defvr

Remote (TRAMP) stores are supported.  On a single-hop ssh-family store,
asynchronous commands run as a local @command{ssh -T} pipe rather than a
TRAMP @code{make-process}, which avoids deadlocking the shared ssh
master.  @code{beads-remote-transport} chooses the transport and
@code{beads-remote-search-path} extends the host's @env{PATH}
(@pxref{User Options}).

@node Dolt and Repositories
@section Dolt and Repositories
@cindex Dolt
@cindex repository

Beads uses Dolt, a version-controlled SQL database, as its backend.
Press @kbd{k} from the dispatch menu for the Dolt menu.

@deffn Command beads-dolt
Open the Dolt database menu: configure the backend, manage the SQL server,
sync with Dolt remotes, and clean up orphaned databases.
@end deffn

@table @asis
@item @strong{Configuration}
@kbd{s} show the current Dolt configuration; @kbd{S} set a configuration
value; @kbd{t} test the connection.
@item @strong{Data}
@kbd{c} commit pending changes to Dolt history; @kbd{p} push commits to
the Dolt remote; @kbd{P} pull commits from the Dolt remote.
@item @strong{Server}
@kbd{1} start the Dolt SQL server; @kbd{0} stop the server; @kbd{i} show
the server status.
@item @strong{Remotes}
@kbd{r} open the remote sub-menu: add (@kbd{a}), list (@kbd{l}), remove
(@kbd{r}), and reset remote data (@kbd{R}).
@item @strong{Maintenance}
@kbd{C} clean up orphaned databases; @kbd{K} kill orphan Dolt server
processes not tracked by the current repository's PID file.
@end table

Repository-level commands (init, branch, worktree, and the Git
integrations) live under @strong{Manage} (@kbd{W} for worktrees) and the
@strong{Setup & migration} group of the maintenance menu
(@pxref{Command and Key Reference}).

@node Configuration
@section Configuration
@cindex configuration
@cindex user options

@deffn Command beads-config
Open the configuration menu: read and write the per-project Beads
configuration.  Press @kbd{.} from the dispatch menu.
@end deffn

Project configuration is stored per project under @file{.beads/}; common
namespaces include @code{jira.*}, @code{linear.*}, @code{github.*}, and
@code{status.*}.

@table @kbd
@item g
Get a value.
@item s
Set a value.
@item S
Set many values at once.
@item l
List all values.
@item u
Unset a value.
@item w
Show the effective configuration.
@item a
Apply (reconcile) the configuration.
@item d
Detect configuration drift.
@item v
Validate the configuration.
@end table

The user options that are not per-project configuration (the executable
path, the actor, the remote transport, and the view limits) are in
@ref{User Options}.

@node Audit and Provenance
@section Audit and Provenance
@cindex audit
@cindex provenance
@cindex history

@deffn Command beads-audit
Open the audit menu (@kbd{@@} in the setup sub-dispatcher): record
(@kbd{r}) and label (@kbd{l}) entries in the
@file{.beads/interactions.jsonl} audit log.
@end deffn

@deffn Command beads-history
Show an issue's history from the @command{bd} journal.  Bound to
@kbd{%} in the maintenance menu.
@end deffn

@deffn Command beads-provenance
Show where a bead came from.  Bound to @kbd{&} in the maintenance menu.
@end deffn

Audit records who changed what and when; provenance records where a bead
came from.  Both are read-only views over the @command{bd} journal.
